  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1221 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nDry air has impeded cloud cover development across much of the \narea early this afternoon, the only exception was across the far \nnorth and across Door County. Temperatures were in the upper 30s \nto middle 40s. For this afternoon, some fair weather cumulus \nis still possible as temperatures rise a few more degrees. For\ntonight, one of the coldest nights so far this fall is expected\nwith lows in the low to middle 20s while readings across the\nDoor peninsula will only fall into the lower to middle 30s.\nNear normal temperatures are expected on Saturday. The main\nconcern for Saturday will be the potential for a low stratus deck\nto develop with return flow. Have trended skies towards mostly \ncloudy, however in the case for tomorrow it will be cloudy if it \ndoes develop which could result in high temperatures being a few \ndegrees cooler.\n\nOtherwise, tranquil conditions to continue through the middle\nof next week. Current forecast is dry, except for a small chance\nof showers on Wednesday. Uncertainty exists on the dry forecast \nfor Thursday and Friday as models suggest some potential for a \nround of rain at some point during this period. After near normal \ntemperatures Saturday, above normal temperatures to continue \nthrough the middle of next week. The latest guidance from the GFS \nwould suggest a cool down for later next week.",
